	(lib_symbols)
	(text "1. Change your default Kicad font to Consolas. Default on Windows, for Mac and Linux, see here: https://gist.github.com/nmcc/4e8ead6c380d8331fedd04e1aa41d351\n	why Consolas? It's a Monospaced font :)\n	to do so, go to Preferences -> Preferences -> Schematic Editor -> Display Options -> Appearance -> Default Font, Consolas.\n2. Fill in the details in the bottom right. Double click the titleblock and see table just above on what to fill in. Check Export to other sheets!\n3. Delete the table.\n4. Set papersize to Letter or A (11\" by 8.5\"). B or C is also allowed, but note that the titleblock will scale down.\n5. Use subsheets. Keep this main sheet (root) and build the rest in subsheets. For small designs, only use the root sheet.\n6. Use Hierarchical labels only. Do not use Global labels.\n\nSome tips:\n- use soft pastel colors for your backgrounds (ChatGPT can help with this)\n- use the correct in/output variation on your hierarchical signals\n- 50 mills text size\n- delete this text :)\n- box on bottom left is exactly half of page in x direction. \n- if you delete subsheets on the root page, the file behind it is not deleted (see your file explorer). Delete the file itself if needed.\n\nif questions, let me know\n- Steyn\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 11.43 18.288 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.905 1.905)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "14a39b0a-53f7-4293-937e-37b0f04901cf")
	)
